OL,3,GNEWSARail disaster of 1957 marked by St
OL,4,AJohn's plaque
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe victims of the Lewisham rail crash
OL,7,Fhave been remembered in a special
OL,8,Fceremony as a commemorative plaque was
OL,9,Funveiled at St John's station.
OL,11,FAn electric train and a steam train
OL,12,Fcollided in thick fog on 4 December
OL,13,F1957, killing 90 people and injuring
OL,14,Fmany more - making it one of the worst
OL,15,Fdisasters in British railway history.
OL,17,FImmediately after the crash, locals
OL,18,Fjoined the relief effort amid harrowing
OL,19,Fscenes, tending to injured passengers
OL,20,Fand taking in those who were stranded.
OL,23,APub: 19-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
